b-authorization-scope walkthrough — worked case (no CLI by design)
Date: 2026-10-09 · Tool versions: n/a (writing exercise) · Environment: local authoring
Fictional engagement: Harborlight Books (invented; no real system involved)

Step 1 — Rules-of-engagement document drafted.
  Checked against the 10-element checklist (parties, objective, in-scope,
  out-of-scope, window, permitted/forbidden techniques, accounts, escalation,
  data handling, termination): 10/10 present and specific.
  In-scope named: portal.harborlight-books.example,
  api.harborlight-books.example/v2, iOS app build 4.2.1.
  Out-of-scope named: payments.harborlight-books.example (third party),
  warehouse inventory system, corporate email.
  Window: 2026-11-03 to 2026-11-14, 18:00-06:00 ET.
  Forbidden: DoS, social engineering, phishing customers, destructive payloads;
  scanning capped at <=10 req/s.
  Accidental-touch procedure: stop, screenshot the request, email named contact
  within one hour. Data destruction within 30 days of engagement end.

Step 2 — Scope-violation triage (5 scenarios), all classified with deciding element:
  1. admin.harborlight-books.example (unnamed) -> OUT. Hard rule 1: a name found
     is a candidate, never permission. Action: do not touch; request written
     amendment if the client wants it covered.
  2. Scanner flags known CVE on in-scope host -> IN SCOPE to observe; NOT a
     finding yet. Hard rules 2 + 6: scanner match is not a new CVE; confirm by
     hand and check reachability before writing up.
  3. Other test user's session token in welcome email -> IN SCOPE event; hard
     rule 4: do NOT use the token. Action: report the token leak as the finding,
     demonstrated with own accounts tester01/tester02.
  4. staging.harborlight-books.example found in JS on in-scope portal -> OUT.
     Hard rule 1. Action: do not probe; note as scope-amendment candidate.
  5. Testing six days after window closed -> OUT. The window is part of the
     authorization. Action: no testing; request a written extension.

Step 3 — Six hard rules written from memory, then verified verbatim against
  brief §7: 6/6 exact on first check.

Step 4 — Self-review: RoE 10/10 elements specific (no "the portal" vagueness);
  triage answers each name deciding element + action. Documents filed as the
  first engagement-record artifacts.

No step marked "not run by us": the work product is writing, and the writing
was done and reviewed in this session.
